SUMMARY:Women in Musical Leadership Masterclass with the TSO: Conducting (
 FREE)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\nWhat exactly is Conducting?\n\n--How d
 oes one learn to Conduct?\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-Could you be an **Orchestra Condu
 ctor**? Interpret a score with your gestures and verbal cues!!\n\nRegister
  for your **FREE** ticket (below)---\n\nWe've attended this in PAST years-
 -with FAB turnout/INTEREST\n\nCreated and run by **Tapestry Opera**\, with
  **lead partner the Toronto Symphony Orchestra\,** *Women in Musical Leade
 rship* is a three-year program designed to collectively develop the next g
 eneration of women and non-binary conductors and music directors in Canada
 .\nWomen in Musical Leadership Conductors work with **Maestro Gustavo** **
 Gimeno** and the musicians of the Toronto Symphony Orchestra in this Maste
 rclass held at Roy Thomson Hall.\n\n\\*\\*\\*During this masterclass\, you
  will observe Women In Musical Leadership Conductors **Monica Chen** and *
 *Eve Legault**\, and Associate Conductor **Serena Reuten** work with TSO M
 usic Director **Gustavo Gimeno** and the world-class TSO. It’s a unique 
 experience that always reveals fascinating details of the conductors’ cr
 aft and offers a peek “behind the scenes” of an orchestra’s rehearsa
 l process.\n\nFREE ticket link here--(please attend if you reserve a ticke
 t)\n\nhttps://tapestryopera.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/events/a0SOF0
 000024Ba12AE\n\nNOTE: this is the SATURDAY morning of the MAY long weekend
 .\n\nCoffee/chat before or afterwards!
