SUMMARY:Toronto Summer Music Festival:  Timothy Chooi (1714 Strad)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\nWe will attend 3 concerts at this year
 's Toronto Summer Music Festival.\n\nYou could use the 10% off promo code 
 for tickets ($30-$80)\n\n**Timothy Chooi\, violin**\n**Jon Kimura Parker\,
  piano**\n\nVitali: Chaconne in G minor\nGluck: “Mélodie” from *Orfeo
  ed Euridice*\nJohn Corigliano: *The Red Violin Caprices*\nFranck: Sonata 
 in A Major for Violin and Piano\n\nA celebration of one of the most iconic
  voices in violin history\, featuring **Timothy Chooi performing on the le
 gendary 1714 “Dolphin” Stradivarius\,** famously played by Jascha Heif
 etz\, alongside the incomparable Jon Kimura Parker. From the electrifying 
 drama of the Vitali Chaconne and the elegance of Gluck’s Mélodie\, to t
 he high-wire brilliance of Corigliano’s *Red Violin Caprices*\, the firs
 t half captures the fire\, precision\, and charisma that defined the Heife
 tz legacy. After intermission\, Franck’s timeless Sonata brings the even
 ing to its emotional summit.\n\n**Ticket link here:**\n\nhttps://torontosu
 mmermusic.com/event/heifetz-the-dolphin-strad/\n\nUse this code for 10% of
 f your ADULT ticket price----CULTURE10
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/toronto-arts-and-culture/events/31383
 1824/
